Patch 7927 (experimental, rollback netcode): write off a queued flip the FIFO walker can never reach, and say where it was.

Two live freezes in online fights on one tester's PC (0.7.0-test1 room 37 and 0.7.0-test3 room 51, both hosting) ended the same way:
flip status WAITING, flips queued = reached + 1, the main thread polling cellGcmGetFlipStatus in the frame pacing (func_006507DC step 1,
lr 0x00650820), no flip for good. The rollback lockstep clock then gives no vblank (correctly) and the game never moves again.
libs/video/cellGcmSys.c: gcm_flip_into_fifo remembers the IO offset of the newest marker it wrote; cellGcm_flip_write_off_lost(want, out)
takes the walker's lock and the flip lock, reports get, put, the marker's offset and the word there now, the flip counters and status,
and with `want` set and the walker idle at put with exactly one flip outstanding counts that flip as reached (what the resync paths
already do for the markers they skip), so the next cellGcmTickFlip completes it. The rollback frame clock (installer/port/jsp/
jsp_stepper.cpp) calls it only after that state has held for a while. No behaviour change: nothing calls it unless the port does.
Test switch GCM_TEST_LOSE_FLIP=<n> (off by default): the walker passes the n-th queued flip without counting it, once, which puts a
fight in exactly that state (two copies on one PC reproduce the freeze, and with the port's recovery, its write-off).
Applies after 7924.

diff --git a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
--- a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
+++ b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
@@ -123,6 +123,7 @@ static volatile int s_flip_pending = 0;
  * executes it; until the drain reaches the marker, the flip has not happened,
  * however many vblanks go by. */
 static volatile u32 s_fifo_flips_queued = 0, s_fifo_flips_reached = 0;
+static volatile u32 s_flip_marker_io = 0xFFFFFFFFu;   /* patch 7927: IO offset of the newest flip marker gcm_flip_into_fifo wrote */
 static u32 s_fifo_flips_completed = 0;   /* reached count at the last completion */
 /* FRAME_TL=1 (diagnostic, off by default): per flip the time from its request (marker queued, guest thread)
  * to the drain reaching it ("draw"), from there to the DONE the guest sees ("tick"), and from that DONE to
@@ -2330,6 +2331,36 @@ void cellGcm_rsx_process_fifo(void)
     }
 }
 
+/* Patch 7927 (rollback netcode): a queued flip the walker can never reach. A guest that polls cellGcmGetFlipStatus for a flip it wrote
+ * into its ring (gcm_flip_into_fifo, "queued") waits forever when the walker has drained everything up to `put` and the flip is still
+ * not "reached": nothing the walker will ever see executes it (two live freezes on one tester's PC, 0.7.0-test1 and test3: queued =
+ * reached + 1, flip status WAITING, main thread in the frame pacing step 1, no flip for good). The frame clock calls this only after it
+ * has seen that state for a while. Under the walker's lock (no pass in flight), `out` (9 words) gets the evidence for the log line:
+ * [0] get, [1] put, [2] the newest marker's IO offset, [3] the word there now (the marker, or what overwrote it), [4] queued,
+ * [5] reached, [6] completed, [7] flip status, [8] 1 = written off. With want_write_off and the walker idle at `put` with exactly one
+ * flip outstanding, that flip counts as reached (as the resync paths do with the flips they skip: "a flip marker skipped here will never
+ * be reached"), so the next cellGcmTickFlip completes it; a marker the walker meets later is not counted twice (the reached != queued
+ * guard). Returns out[8]. */
+int cellGcm_flip_write_off_lost(int want_write_off, uint32_t* out)
+{
+    AcquireSRWLockExclusive(&s_gcm_fifo_lock);
+    FLIP_LOCK();
+    const u32 put = vm_read32(GCM_CONTROL_GUEST_ADDR + 0);
+    const u32 mio = s_flip_marker_io;
+    const u32 mea = mio != 0xFFFFFFFFu ? gcm_io2ea(mio) : 0;
+    out[0] = s_fifo_getoff; out[1] = put; out[2] = mio; out[3] = mea ? vm_read32(mea) : 0xFFFFFFFFu;
+    out[4] = s_fifo_flips_queued; out[5] = s_fifo_flips_reached; out[6] = s_fifo_flips_completed; out[7] = (u32)s_flip_status;
+    out[8] = 0;
+    if (want_write_off && s_fifo_getoff == put && s_flip_status == CELL_GCM_FLIP_STATUS_WAITING &&
+        s_fifo_flips_queued == s_fifo_flips_reached + 1u && s_fifo_flips_reached == s_fifo_flips_completed) {
+        s_fifo_flips_reached = s_fifo_flips_queued;
+        out[8] = 1;
+    }
+    FLIP_UNLOCK();
+    ReleaseSRWLockExclusive(&s_gcm_fifo_lock);
+    return (int)out[8];
+}
+
 /* The methods rsx_process_method acts on beyond its own rsx_state: the notify
  * and semaphore DMA contexts, the notify write, the back-end label offset and
  * label writes, and SET_REFERENCE (g_rsx_last_reference). Everything else only
@@ -2721,6 +2752,13 @@ static void gcm_rsx_process_fifo_unlocked(void)
                 s_flip_request_count++;
                 /* Not past `queued`: a resync may already have written off
                  * this flip. */
+                /* Patch 7927 test switch GCM_TEST_LOSE_FLIP=<n> (off by default): the walker passes the n-th queued flip without
+                 * counting it, once -- the state of the live freezes (queued = reached + 1, get == put), for testing the recovery. */
+                static long lose_at = -1; if (lose_at < 0) { const char* e = getenv("GCM_TEST_LOSE_FLIP"); lose_at = e ? atol(e) : 0; }
+                if (lose_at > 0 && s_fifo_flips_reached + 1u == (u32)lose_at) {
+                    lose_at = 0;
+                    fprintf(stderr, "[cellGcmSys] GCM_TEST_LOSE_FLIP: flip %u passed without counting it (test)\n", s_fifo_flips_reached + 1u);
+                } else
                 if (s_fifo_flips_reached != s_fifo_flips_queued) { s_fifo_flips_reached++; ftl_reach(s_fifo_flips_reached); }
             } else {
                 cellGcmSetFlipCommand(w & 0xFFu);
@@ -3665,6 +3703,7 @@ static int gcm_flip_into_fifo(u32 ctx, u32 bufferId)
     const u32 end = vm_read32(ctx + 4), cur = vm_read32(ctx + 8);
     if (gcm_ea2io(cur) == 0xFFFFFFFFu) return 0;
     vm_write32(cur, GCM_FLIP_MARKER | bufferId);
